import Hdl.Core
import Hdl.Temporal
/-!
# Hdl.Formal: SVA-style formal harnesses for emitted Verilog

`import Hdl.Formal` turns a `Circuit` and a list of declared properties into Verilog with
an `` `ifdef FORMAL `` harness: the properties become immediate assertions (`assert`,
`assume`, `cover`) clocked by the design's clock, with `$past`, `$stable`, `$rose` and
`$fell`, and `(* anyconst *)` declarations for symbolic constants. The harness is the
external-checking side of `lib/Hdl/Temporal.wiz`: each constructor says which `TL`
formula it is (over the design's observation trace), and the emitted check is the same
formula on the Verilog signals. A kernel proof is still what `Hdl.Temporal` gives; this
lets SymbiYosys (`sby`) or `yosys-smtbmc` discharge the same property without one.

The non-formal text is unchanged: `Verilog.emit` does not include the harness, and every
line this module adds is inside `` `ifdef FORMAL ``.

```
import IO
import Hdl.Formal
def c : Circuit Bit Bit := Circuit.delay Bit (BitVec.ofNat 1 0)
def p : FProp := FProp.mk "delay" (FKind.impliesNext (FTerm.inp "x") (FTerm.outp "y"))
IO.writeFile "delay.v" (Verilog.emitFormal "delay" c [p])
IO.writeFile "delay.sby" (Formal.sby "delay.v" "delay" "bmc" 8)
```

The property language is deliberately a *monitor* language, not all of `TL`: quantifier
nesting, unbounded liveness (`◇`), `until` and SVA sequences/`##[m:n]` are not emitted
yet (see "Gaps" in the module docs). What is emitted maps one-to-one onto the usual
`ifdef FORMAL` idioms, so the harness is readable and every line has a `TL` reading:

| constructor | `TL` reading | emitted check |
|---|---|---|
| `FKind.always t` | `□ (nowB t)` | `always @(posedge clk) assert (t);` |
| `FKind.implies a t` | `□ (a |-> t)` | `assert (!(a) || (t));` |
| `FKind.impliesNext a t` | `□ (a |=> t)` | `assert (!$past(a) \|\| t);` |
| `FKind.nexts n t` | `□ (○ⁿ t)` | `assert (t);` from cycle `n` on |
| `FKind.cover t` | `◇ (nowB t)` | `cover (t);` |
| `FKind.assumeAlways t` | environment | `assume (t);` |
| `FKind.assumeInitial t` | reset convention | `initial assume (t);` |
| `FKind.assumeImplies a t` | environment | `assume (!(a) \|\| t);` |
| `FKind.assumeImpliesNext a t` | environment | `assume (!$past(a) \|\| t);` |

`assert`/`assume`/`cover` are checked by yosys's formal front end (`read_verilog
-formal`); they are inside `` `ifdef FORMAL ``, so synthesis and simulation of the module
are untouched. The harness keeps a small saturating cycle counter and gates a check that
needs history until the history exists, so `$past` is never read before cycle 0 (which is
otherwise an unconstrained value and a spurious failure).

## Gaps

* SVA operators beyond the table: `##[m:n]`, `[*n]`, `throughout`, `until`, `s_eventually`
  and multi-clock properties. The `TL` layer has `until`, `delayRange`, `within` and
  fairness; their emission needs a proper SVA sequence printer (yosys 0.70 does not
  parse `|->` itself, so the current encoding is immediate assertions).
* Liveness (`TL.eventually`, `TL.leadsTo`, `TL.infOften`, `TL.WF`) is not emitted:
  BMC and k-induction prove safety, not liveness; a liveness proof needs a lasso or a
  ranking argument, and would be a different `.sby` engine.
* Datapath terms are not type checked against the circuit's `HwTy`: a name that is not
  a port renders as `?`, which yosys rejects, instead of failing the Wiz program. (A
  typed term layer over `HwTy.leaves` would fix that.)
* One harness per module, on the first clock domain; multi-clock assumptions
  (`set_clock_groups`) belong to `Hdl.Xdc`, not to this module.
-/

------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Terms (the data expressions of a property)

/-- A term over the emitted module's signals: ports by their `HwTy.portNames` name, a
literal, an `(* anyconst *)` symbolic constant, or an operator. The width of a term is
Verilog's (it is not tracked here); literals carry theirs. `not`, `and`, `or` and `xor`
are bitwise; `slice` is a part select of a *reference* (a port or constant), not of an
arbitrary expression. -/
inductive FTerm where
  | inp (name : String)
  | outp (name : String)
  | lit (w v : Nat)
  | anyc (name : String) (w : Nat)
  | not (a : FTerm)
  | and (a b : FTerm)
  | or (a b : FTerm)
  | xor (a b : FTerm)
  | eq (a b : FTerm)
  | ne (a b : FTerm)
  | ult (a b : FTerm)
  | slt (a b : FTerm)
  | add (a b : FTerm)
  | sub (a b : FTerm)
  | mul (a b : FTerm)
  | cat (a b : FTerm)
  | mux (c a b : FTerm)
  | slice (a : FTerm) (lo w : Nat)
  | past (n : Nat) (a : FTerm)
  | stable (n : Nat) (a : FTerm)
  | rose (a : FTerm)
  | fell (a : FTerm)

/-- A symbolic constant: one value for the whole proof, chosen freely, declared
`(* anyconst *)`. Two terms with the same name are the same constant. -/
def FTerm.const (name : String) (w : Nat) : FTerm := FTerm.anyc name w

------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Properties (the checks a harness emits)

/-- The kind of a monitor. Each is a `TL` formula over the design's observation trace;
see the table in the module docs. -/
inductive FKind where
  | always (t : FTerm)
  | implies (a t : FTerm)
  | impliesNext (a t : FTerm)
  | nexts (n : Nat) (t : FTerm)
  | cover (t : FTerm)
  | assumeAlways (t : FTerm)
  | assumeInitial (t : FTerm)
  | assumeImplies (a t : FTerm)
  | assumeImpliesNext (a t : FTerm)

/-- A named monitor: the name is a comment in the harness and the label a solver prints
with a counterexample. -/
structure FProp where
  name : String
  kind : FKind

/-- `□ t`, an invariant. -/
def FProp.always (name : String) (t : FTerm) : FProp := FProp.mk name (FKind.always t)
/-- `□ (a |-> t)`, an implication checked in the same cycle. -/
def FProp.implies (name : String) (a t : FTerm) : FProp := FProp.mk name (FKind.implies a t)
/-- `□ (a |=> t)`, an implication checked in the next cycle (`$past(a)`). -/
def FProp.impliesNext (name : String) (a t : FTerm) : FProp := FProp.mk name (FKind.impliesNext a t)
/-- `□ (○ⁿ t)`, `t` at every cycle from `n` on (checked at each cycle `≥ n`). -/
def FProp.nexts (name : String) (n : Nat) (t : FTerm) : FProp := FProp.mk name (FKind.nexts n t)
/-- A reachability target (`cover`), not an assertion. -/
def FProp.cover (name : String) (t : FTerm) : FProp := FProp.mk name (FKind.cover t)
/-- An environment assumption at every cycle. -/
def FProp.assumeAlways (name : String) (t : FTerm) : FProp := FProp.mk name (FKind.assumeAlways t)
/-- A reset/initial-state assumption: `initial assume (t);`. -/
def FProp.assumeInitial (name : String) (t : FTerm) : FProp := FProp.mk name (FKind.assumeInitial t)
/-- An environment assumption `□ (a |-> t)`. -/
def FProp.assumeImplies (name : String) (a t : FTerm) : FProp :=
  FProp.mk name (FKind.assumeImplies a t)
/-- An environment assumption `□ (a |=> t)`. -/
def FProp.assumeImpliesNext (name : String) (a t : FTerm) : FProp :=
  FProp.mk name (FKind.assumeImpliesNext a t)

------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Widths, depths and names

/-- The bits needed for `n`: `Nat.log2 n + 1` (`1` for `0` and `1`, `2` for `2`–`3`, …). -/
def Formal.needBits (n : Nat) : Nat := Nat.succ (Nat.log2 n)
/-- The width of the harness's cycle counter for a maximum history depth of `n`. -/
def Formal.cycleWidth (n : Nat) : Nat := Formal.needBits n

/-- How many cycles of history a term reads (`$past` depth; nested `$past`s add). -/
def Formal.termDepth : FTerm → Nat
  | .not a => Formal.termDepth a
  | .and a b => Nat.max (Formal.termDepth a) (Formal.termDepth b)
  | .or a b => Nat.max (Formal.termDepth a) (Formal.termDepth b)
  | .xor a b => Nat.max (Formal.termDepth a) (Formal.termDepth b)
  | .eq a b => Nat.max (Formal.termDepth a) (Formal.termDepth b)
  | .ne a b => Nat.max (Formal.termDepth a) (Formal.termDepth b)
  | .ult a b => Nat.max (Formal.termDepth a) (Formal.termDepth b)
  | .slt a b => Nat.max (Formal.termDepth a) (Formal.termDepth b)
  | .add a b => Nat.max (Formal.termDepth a) (Formal.termDepth b)
  | .sub a b => Nat.max (Formal.termDepth a) (Formal.termDepth b)
  | .mul a b => Nat.max (Formal.termDepth a) (Formal.termDepth b)
  | .cat a b => Nat.max (Formal.termDepth a) (Formal.termDepth b)
  | .mux c a b => Nat.max (Formal.termDepth c) (Nat.max (Formal.termDepth a) (Formal.termDepth b))
  | .slice a _ _ => Formal.termDepth a
  | .past n a => Nat.add n (Formal.termDepth a)
  | .stable n a => Nat.add n (Formal.termDepth a)
  | .rose a => Nat.succ (Formal.termDepth a)
  | .fell a => Nat.succ (Formal.termDepth a)
  | _ => 0

/-- How many cycles of history a monitor reads. -/
def Formal.kindDepth : FKind → Nat
  | .always t => Formal.termDepth t
  | .implies a t => Nat.max (Formal.termDepth a) (Formal.termDepth t)
  | .impliesNext a t => Nat.max (Nat.succ (Formal.termDepth a)) (Formal.termDepth t)
  | .nexts n t => Nat.max n (Formal.termDepth t)
  | .cover t => Formal.termDepth t
  | .assumeAlways t => Formal.termDepth t
  | .assumeInitial t => 0
  | .assumeImplies a t => Nat.max (Formal.termDepth a) (Formal.termDepth t)
  | .assumeImpliesNext a t => Nat.max (Nat.succ (Formal.termDepth a)) (Formal.termDepth t)

/-- The history depth a list of monitors needs (the counter saturates there). -/
def Formal.propsDepth : List FProp → Nat
  | .nil => 0
  | .cons p ps => Nat.max (Formal.kindDepth p.kind) (Formal.propsDepth ps)

/-- Add a symbolic constant to a list unless its name is already there. -/
def Formal.addConst (c : String × Nat) : List (String × Nat) → List (String × Nat)
  | .nil => .cons c .nil
  | .cons d ds => match Hdl.strEq c.1 d.1 with
    | .true => .cons d ds
    | .false => .cons d (Formal.addConst c ds)

/-- The symbolic constants of a term, in order. -/
def Formal.termConsts (t : FTerm) (acc : List (String × Nat)) : List (String × Nat) := match t with
  | .anyc name w => Formal.addConst (name, w) acc
  | .not a => Formal.termConsts a acc
  | .and a b => Formal.termConsts b (Formal.termConsts a acc)
  | .or a b => Formal.termConsts b (Formal.termConsts a acc)
  | .xor a b => Formal.termConsts b (Formal.termConsts a acc)
  | .eq a b => Formal.termConsts b (Formal.termConsts a acc)
  | .ne a b => Formal.termConsts b (Formal.termConsts a acc)
  | .ult a b => Formal.termConsts b (Formal.termConsts a acc)
  | .slt a b => Formal.termConsts b (Formal.termConsts a acc)
  | .add a b => Formal.termConsts b (Formal.termConsts a acc)
  | .sub a b => Formal.termConsts b (Formal.termConsts a acc)
  | .mul a b => Formal.termConsts b (Formal.termConsts a acc)
  | .cat a b => Formal.termConsts b (Formal.termConsts a acc)
  | .mux c a b => Formal.termConsts b (Formal.termConsts a (Formal.termConsts c acc))
  | .slice a _ _ => Formal.termConsts a acc
  | .past _ a => Formal.termConsts a acc
  | .stable _ a => Formal.termConsts a acc
  | .rose a => Formal.termConsts a acc
  | .fell a => Formal.termConsts a acc
  | _ => acc

/-- The symbolic constants of a monitor. -/
def Formal.kindConsts (k : FKind) (acc : List (String × Nat)) : List (String × Nat) := match k with
  | .always t => Formal.termConsts t acc
  | .implies a t => Formal.termConsts t (Formal.termConsts a acc)
  | .impliesNext a t => Formal.termConsts t (Formal.termConsts a acc)
  | .nexts _ t => Formal.termConsts t acc
  | .cover t => Formal.termConsts t acc
  | .assumeAlways t => Formal.termConsts t acc
  | .assumeInitial t => Formal.termConsts t acc
  | .assumeImplies a t => Formal.termConsts t (Formal.termConsts a acc)
  | .assumeImpliesNext a t => Formal.termConsts t (Formal.termConsts a acc)

/-- The symbolic constants of a list of monitors, first occurrence wins. -/
def Formal.propsConsts : List FProp → List (String × Nat) → List (String × Nat)
  | .nil, acc => acc
  | .cons p ps, acc => Formal.propsConsts ps (Formal.kindConsts p.kind acc)

/-- Look a constant's Verilog name up. -/
def Formal.constName (name : String) : List (String × String) → String
  | .nil => "?"
  | .cons c cs => match Hdl.strEq c.1 name with
    | .true => c.2
    | .false => Formal.constName name cs

/-- The Verilog identifiers of the symbolic constants, allocated fresh after the module's
own names. -/
def Formal.constIdents : List (String × Nat) → Hdl.Set → List (String × String) × Hdl.Set
  | .nil, used => (.nil, used)
  | .cons c cs, used =>
    let ω r := Verilog.fresh used ("f_" <+> c.1);
    let ω rest := Formal.constIdents cs r.2;
    (.cons (c.1, r.1) rest.1, rest.2)

/-- The port index of a name in a list of ports (`0` if it is not there). -/
def Formal.portIndex (name : String) : List NetPort → Nat → Nat
  | .nil, _ => 0
  | .cons p ps, k => match Hdl.strEq p.name name with
    | .true => k
    | .false => Formal.portIndex name ps (Nat.succ k)

/-- Whether a name is a port of a list. -/
def Formal.hasPort (name : String) : List NetPort → Bool
  | .nil => .false
  | .cons p ps => match Hdl.strEq p.name name with
    | .true => .true
    | .false => Formal.hasPort name ps

/-- The Verilog reference for an input port name (`_`-prefixed and `?` if absent). -/
def Formal.inputRef (n : Netlist) (vn : VNames) (name : String) : String :=
  match Formal.hasPort name n.inputs with
  | .true => Hdl.nthD "?" vn.ins (Formal.portIndex name n.inputs 0)
  | .false => "?"

/-- The Verilog reference for an output port name. -/
def Formal.outputRef (n : Netlist) (vn : VNames) (name : String) : String :=
  match Formal.hasPort name n.outputs with
  | .true => Hdl.nthD "?" vn.outs (Formal.portIndex name n.outputs 0)
  | .false => "?"

/-- What rendering a term needs: the netlist, its port identifiers and the symbolic
constant names. -/
structure Formal.Fcx where
  n : Netlist
  vn : VNames
  consts : List (String × String)

/-- The Verilog text of a term. -/
def Formal.termText (cx : Formal.Fcx) : FTerm → String
  | .inp name => Formal.inputRef cx.n cx.vn name
  | .outp name => Formal.outputRef cx.n cx.vn name
  | .lit w v => Verilog.lit w v
  | .anyc name _ => Formal.constName name cx.consts
  | .not a => "~(" <+> Formal.termText cx a <+> ")"
  | .and a b => "(" <+> Formal.termText cx a <+> " & " <+> Formal.termText cx b <+> ")"
  | .or a b => "(" <+> Formal.termText cx a <+> " | " <+> Formal.termText cx b <+> ")"
  | .xor a b => "(" <+> Formal.termText cx a <+> " ^ " <+> Formal.termText cx b <+> ")"
  | .eq a b => "(" <+> Formal.termText cx a <+> " == " <+> Formal.termText cx b <+> ")"
  | .ne a b => "(" <+> Formal.termText cx a <+> " != " <+> Formal.termText cx b <+> ")"
  | .ult a b => "(" <+> Formal.termText cx a <+> " < " <+> Formal.termText cx b <+> ")"
  | .slt a b =>
    "($signed(" <+> Formal.termText cx a <+> ") < $signed(" <+> Formal.termText cx b <+> "))"
  | .add a b => "(" <+> Formal.termText cx a <+> " + " <+> Formal.termText cx b <+> ")"
  | .sub a b => "(" <+> Formal.termText cx a <+> " - " <+> Formal.termText cx b <+> ")"
  | .mul a b => "(" <+> Formal.termText cx a <+> " * " <+> Formal.termText cx b <+> ")"
  | .cat a b => "{" <+> Formal.termText cx a <+> ", " <+> Formal.termText cx b <+> "}"
  | .mux c a b =>
    "(" <+> Formal.termText cx c <+> " ? " <+> Formal.termText cx a <+> " : " <+> Formal.termText cx b <+> ")"
  | .slice a lo w =>
    Formal.termText cx a <+> "[" <+> Hdl.show (lo + w - 1) <+> ":" <+> Hdl.show lo <+> "]"
  | .past n a => "$past(" <+> Formal.termText cx a <+> ", " <+> Hdl.show n <+> ")"
  | .stable n a => match n with
    | .succ .zero => "$stable(" <+> Formal.termText cx a <+> ")"
    | .zero => "1'd1"
    | _ =>
      "(" <+> Formal.termText cx a <+> " == $past(" <+> Formal.termText cx a <+> ", " <+> Hdl.show n <+> "))"
  | .rose a => "$rose(" <+> Formal.termText cx a <+> ")"
  | .fell a => "$fell(" <+> Formal.termText cx a <+> ")"

/-- A term as a Verilog boolean: its bits are true when nonzero, so `(t)` itself is the
test (`!` is Verilog's logical not, which makes a one-bit result). -/
def Formal.testText (cx : Formal.Fcx) (t : FTerm) : String := "(" <+> Formal.termText cx t <+> ")"

/-- A statement guarded by the cycle counter: it runs only once the history it reads
exists (`depth` cycles). With no history, the statement runs unconditionally. -/
def Formal.gate (cyc : String) (depth : Nat) (body : String) : String := match depth with
  | .zero => body
  | .succ _ =>
    "if (" <+> cyc <+> " >= " <+> Verilog.lit (Formal.cycleWidth depth) depth <+> ") " <+> body

/-- `assert (body);`, gated by `depth`. -/
def Formal.assertAt (cyc : String) (depth : Nat) (body : String) : String :=
  Formal.gate cyc depth ("assert (" <+> body <+> ");")
/-- `assume (body);`, gated by `depth`. -/
def Formal.assumeAt (cyc : String) (depth : Nat) (body : String) : String :=
  Formal.gate cyc depth ("assume (" <+> body <+> ");")
/-- `cover (body);`, gated by `depth`. -/
def Formal.coverAt (cyc : String) (depth : Nat) (body : String) : String :=
  Formal.gate cyc depth ("cover (" <+> body <+> ");")

/-- The assertion/assumption text of a monitor kind, without the surrounding `always`.
`off` is the cycle at which history starts (1 when the design has a reset: cycle 0 is the
reset cycle, so a relation that looks at an edge must not start there). -/
def Formal.kindText (cx : Formal.Fcx) (cyc : String) (off : Nat) (k : FKind) : String :=
  let d := Nat.add off (Formal.kindDepth k);
  match k with
  | .always t => Formal.assertAt cyc d (Formal.testText cx t)
  | .implies a t =>
    Formal.assertAt cyc d ("!" <+> Formal.testText cx a <+> " || " <+> Formal.testText cx t)
  | .impliesNext a t =>
    Formal.assertAt cyc d ("!$past(" <+> Formal.termText cx a <+> ") || " <+> Formal.testText cx t)
  | .nexts _ t => Formal.assertAt cyc d (Formal.testText cx t)
  | .cover t => Formal.coverAt cyc d (Formal.testText cx t)
  | .assumeAlways t => Formal.assumeAt cyc d (Formal.testText cx t)
  | .assumeInitial t => Formal.assumeAt cyc d (Formal.testText cx t)
  | .assumeImplies a t =>
    Formal.assumeAt cyc d ("!" <+> Formal.testText cx a <+> " || " <+> Formal.testText cx t)
  | .assumeImpliesNext a t =>
    Formal.assumeAt cyc d ("!$past(" <+> Formal.termText cx a <+> ") || " <+> Formal.testText cx t)

/-- The words of a kind, for the harness comment. -/
def Formal.kindWord : FKind → String
  | .always _ => "always"
  | .implies _ _ => "implies"
  | .impliesNext _ _ => "impliesNext"
  | .nexts n _ => "nexts " <+> Hdl.show n
  | .cover _ => "cover"
  | .assumeAlways _ => "assumeAlways"
  | .assumeInitial _ => "assumeInitial"
  | .assumeImplies _ _ => "assumeImplies"
  | .assumeImpliesNext _ _ => "assumeImpliesNext"

/-- The line(s) of one monitor: a comment naming it, then the check (an `initial
assume` for `assumeInitial`, a clocked statement for everything else). -/
def Formal.propText (cx : Formal.Fcx) (cyc : String) (clk : String) (off : Nat) (p : FProp) : String :=
  let ω head := "  // [" <+> p.name <+> "] " <+> Formal.kindWord p.kind <+> "\n";
  head <+> match p.kind with
    | .assumeInitial t => "  initial assume (" <+> Formal.testText cx t <+> ");\n"
    | _ => "  always @(posedge " <+> clk <+> ") " <+> Formal.kindText cx cyc off p.kind <+> "\n"

/-- The blocks of a list of monitors. -/
def Formal.propsText (cx : Formal.Fcx) (cyc : String) (clk : String) (off : Nat) : List FProp → String
  | .nil => ""
  | .cons p ps => Formal.propText cx cyc clk off p <+> Formal.propsText cx cyc clk off ps

/-- The `(* anyconst *)` declarations. -/
def Formal.constDecls (nms : List (String × String)) (cs : List (String × Nat)) : String :=
  match nms, cs with
  | .cons nm nms', .cons c cs' =>
    "  (* anyconst *) reg " <+> Verilog.range c.2 <+> nm.2 <+> ";\n" <+> Formal.constDecls nms' cs'
  | _, _ => ""

/-- The cycle counter: `f_cycle` counts clock edges up to `max` and then holds, so a
check can require that its `$past` history exists. -/
def Formal.cycleDecl (cyc clk : String) (max : Nat) : String :=
  match max with
  | .zero => ""
  | .succ _ =>
    let ω w := Formal.cycleWidth max;
    "  reg " <+> Verilog.range w <+> cyc <+> " = " <+> Verilog.lit w 0 <+> ";\n" <+> "  always @(posedge " <+> clk <+> ") if (" <+> cyc <+> " != " <+> Verilog.lit w max <+> ") " <+> cyc <+> " <= " <+> cyc <+> " + " <+> Verilog.lit w 1 <+> ";\n"

/-- The width of a port name, or `0`. -/
def Formal.portWidth (name : String) : List NetPort → Nat
  | .nil => 0
  | .cons p ps => match Hdl.strEq p.name name with
    | .true => p.width
    | .false => Formal.portWidth name ps

/-- The names already used by the emitted module's wires, ports and registers. The
harness's own names are fresh against them as well as against `VNames.used` (which covers
only ports, registers and memories; `Verilog.ctx` also names the wires). -/
def Formal.refNames (cx : VCtx) : Nat → Hdl.Set → Hdl.Set
  | .zero, s => s
  | .succ k, s =>
    let ω nm := VCtx.ref cx k;
    Formal.refNames cx k (HTrie.put (Hdl.strKey nm) () s)

/-- The reset input's Verilog reference, if the circuit has a one-bit `rst` port. -/
def Formal.resetRef (n : Netlist) (vn : VNames) : Option String :=
  match Formal.hasPort "rst" n.inputs, Formal.portWidth "rst" n.inputs with
  | .true, .succ .zero => .some (Formal.inputRef n vn "rst")
  | _, _ => .none

/-- The first clock domain's Verilog net (`clk` when there is none). -/
def Formal.clockOf (n : Netlist) : String := match n.clocks with
  | .nil => "clk"
  | .cons d _ => d.name

/-- The harness block: an `` `ifdef FORMAL `` region to put before `endmodule`, with the
cycle counter, symbolic constants, the reset assumption and one clocked check per
monitor. -/
def Formal.block (n : Netlist) (vn : VNames) (vcx : VCtx) (props : List FProp) : String :=
  let ω reset := Formal.resetRef n vn;
  let ω off := match reset with
    | .some _ => 1
    | .none => 0;
  let ω depth := Nat.add off (Formal.propsDepth props);
  let ω clk := Formal.clockOf n;
  let ω used := Formal.refNames vcx vcx.names.count vn.used;
  let ω cycR := Verilog.fresh used "f_cycle";
  let ω cs := Formal.propsConsts props [];
  let ω ids := Formal.constIdents cs cycR.2;
  let ω cx := Formal.Fcx.mk n vn ids.1;
  "\n`ifdef FORMAL\n" <+> "  // Hdl.Formal harness: " <+> Hdl.show (List.length props) <+> " monitor(s) on posedge " <+> clk <+> ", history depth " <+> Hdl.show depth <+> ".\n" <+> Formal.cycleDecl cycR.1 clk depth <+> Formal.constDecls ids.1 cs <+> (match reset with
    | .some rst =>
      "  // reset is asserted in the first cycle and not again: the environment the\n" <+> "  // properties are stated for (a design that needs a longer reset says so).\n" <+> "  initial assume (" <+> rst <+> ");\n" <+> "  always @(posedge " <+> clk <+> ") if (" <+> cycR.1 <+> " >= 1'd1) assume (~" <+> rst <+> ");\n"
    | .none => "") <+> Formal.propsText cx cycR.1 clk off props <+> "`endif\n"

------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Emission

/-- A circuit's Verilog with an `` `ifdef FORMAL `` harness for `props`. The text outside
the `ifdef` is exactly `Verilog.emit`'s. -/
def Verilog.emitFormal {ω i o : HwTy} (name : String) (c : Circuit i o) (props : List FProp) : String :=
  let ω n := Circuit.netlist name c;
  let ω vn := Verilog.portIdents n;
  let ω cx := Verilog.ctx n vn;
  Verilog.moduleText n vn cx <+> Formal.block n vn cx props <+> "endmodule\n"

/-- An `` `ifdef FORMAL `` harness for an existing netlist (the emission entry point when
the netlist was built with `Circuit.netlistS` or `Multi.netlist`). -/
def Verilog.emitFormalN (n : Netlist) (props : List FProp) : String :=
  let ω vn := Verilog.portIdents n;
  let ω cx := Verilog.ctx n vn;
  Verilog.moduleText n vn cx <+> Formal.block n vn cx props <+> "endmodule\n"

/-- A SymbiYosys job file for an emitted harness: `mode` is `bmc` or `prove`, `depth`
its bound (or induction depth). Run `sby -f <name>.sby`. -/
def Formal.sby (file top mode : String) (depth : Nat) : String :=
  "[options]\n" <+> "mode " <+> mode <+> "\n" <+> "depth " <+> Hdl.show depth <+> "\n" <+> "\n[engines]\n" <+> "smtbmc\n" <+> "\n[script]\n" <+> "read -formal " <+> file <+> "\n" <+> "prep -top " <+> Verilog.ident top <+> "\n" <+> "\n[files]\n" <+> file <+> "\n"
